Decisions + contract notes
- SHA-256 implemented in-tree (rig/package/sha256.hpp, new header in own dir): no crypto lib on the allowed list.
- to_yaml is a hand-written emitter (not YAML::Emitter): content_hash must not depend on the yaml-cpp version.
- Numbers/booleans must be plain YAML scalars: `fps: "60"` is a type error. Booleans: true/false only (no yes/no).
- Sensor-mode legality checked only for argus/gst backends (mock/replay synthesize any size). Ultrawide role must
  use a full-FOV mode; main may use 16:9 crops. Nominal tables in common/config/sensor_modes.cpp [I]; reviewer:
  cross-check with T2's mode tables.
- imu.noise.* are REQUIRED (feed SLAM settings). live_checks / slam_live cross-checks (camera ids exist, fps
  thresholds below camera fps, vocabulary path for orbslam3) run even when the section is omitted.
- shm writer liveness = F_OFD_SETLK lock held for the writer's life (kernel drops it on any death; no pid
  reuse issue); readers/new writers probe with F_OFD_GETLK. writer_alive() = pid exists && lock held && the name
  still maps to the reader's inode. Same semantics as the frozen comment (which mentions kill(pid,0)).
- Seqlock writer uses relaxed odd store + release fence (Boehm 2012); reader copies with relaxed atomic word loads
  in a no_sanitize_thread function (benign race, validated by the seq re-check). Torture test: ~3M msgs, 0 torn.
- encode_frame copies planes TIGHTLY; slot size = sizeof(ShmFrameHeader) + frame_payload_bytes(w,h,fmt).
- StreamSubscription destructor marks its queue detached: the hub skips it, so a dropped lossless subscription
  never latches lossless_overflow; stats() lists only live subscribers.
- CONTRACT NOTE (private members only): Session gained private camera_ids_ / imu_id_ (read from the frozen
  rig.yaml) so create_package() makes raw/cam_<id>/frames and raw/<imu id>/. No public declaration changed.
- Layout constants (rig/package/layout.hpp) fix the exact CSV headers T5 must write: cam data.csv = EuRoC
  "#timestamp [ns],filename"; imu data.csv = EuRoC header; chip.csv = brackets (t_host_before_ns,chip_ticks,
  t_host_after_ns) per T0; per-sample chip ticks/temp/flags go to OPTIONAL imu0/sample_meta.csv (reviewer/T5:
  confirm). frame_meta.csv / drops.csv / live_slam.csv headers defined there.
- derive_state: skipped == passed; failed validate_raw or validate -> invalid; other failures keep the state.
- Session::create builds in a hidden temp dir and publishes with renameat2(RENAME_NOREPLACE); Session::open
  re-hashes rig.yaml and refuses a modified frozen config (kDataLoss). create_package writes manifest LAST.
- discard(): logs -> aborted/<name>/ (fsync) -> rename pkg to .trash-<name> -> delete.
- Manifest/session JSON: unknown keys rejected (kDataLoss); times kInvalidTime <-> null; "state" written for
  humans, ignored on read.
- Camera ids must also be <= 15 chars (ShmFrameHeader::camera_id is char[16]).

